  "name": "Lunisolar (Metonic)",
  "description": "A lunisolar example on the 19-year Metonic cycle (235 months, 6940 days): months alternate 30 and 29 days from the First Moon; common years have 12 months (354 days, or 355 in the full years 1, 5, 10 and 15 of the cycle, whose Twelfth Moon has 30 days), and years 3, 6, 8, 11, 14, 17 and 19 add a 30-day Leap Moon (384 days). Astronomical years, no eras.",
  "origin": "the start of the First Moon 1, year 1 (the first year of a cycle)",
